# Build context excludes. Anything not needed INSIDE the image belongs here — the context is
# transferred to the daemon before the first instruction runs, so a stray cache directory is paid
# for on every build.
#
# `.turbo` is the one that bit: it reached 51GB locally and, being unlisted, was streamed into the
# build until the Docker daemon fell over. Caches are rebuilt on demand and must never be shipped.
.git
.github
.turbo
**/.turbo
.codex-temp
.pnpm-store
tmp
**/.next
**/.terraform
**/coverage
**/dist
**/node_modules
_review_shots
docs
infra
team
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.env
.env.*

# …except the OpenAPI artifact, which the api build copies into `dist/` so the running container can
# serve it. Excluding all of `docs` is why the deployed `/docs/openapi.json` answered 503
# `openapi_artifact_missing`: the file is committed and tracked, and simply never entered the image.
# .dockerignore takes the LAST matching pattern, so this re-include must stay below `docs`.
!docs/api/openapi.internal.json
